A value whose Jinja does not parse fails the same way as a bad macro path — the template
error is reported against the offending value, never as a traceback.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
---
# Body
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md x="{{ macro( }}"
-- exit --
2
-- stdout --
-- stderr --
error: value '{{ macro( }}': TemplateSyntaxError: unexpected '}', expected ')'
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
---
# Body
